{{!
    @template mod_rememberme/mobile_view

    The study session as shown in the Moodle app.

    The question is rendered by the app's own core-question component, which is
    exported to site plugins. It receives the server rendered question and turns
    it into native controls via the app's question type handlers, so this
    template does not need to know one question type from another.

    The question binding is guarded, because the template is compiled before the
    accompanying JavaScript has parsed it out of CONTENT_OTHERDATA.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * cmid Number The course module id
    * name String The activity name
    * hasquestion Boolean Whether a question is being presented
    * haschoices Boolean Whether the question is presented as tappable options
    * message String Shown when there is no question to answer
    * due Number Items a session would offer right now
    * answered Number Questions answered so far in this session
    * total Number Questions in this session
    * weekdone Number Items completed this week
    * weektarget Number This week's frozen target
    * streak Number Consecutive weeks cleared
    * hasstreak Boolean Whether to show the streak

    Example context (json):
    {
        "cmid": 42,
        "name": "Vocabulary review",
        "hasquestion": true,
        "haschoices": false,
        "message": "",
        "due": 12,
        "answered": 3,
        "total": 20,
        "weekdone": 8,
        "weektarget": 20,
        "streak": 3,
        "hasstreak": true
    }
}}
<div>
    <ion-card>
        <ion-card-content>
            <ion-chip color="primary">
                <ion-label>{{weekdone}} / {{weektarget}} {{#str}} weekprogresslabel, mod_rememberme {{/str}}</ion-label>
            </ion-chip>
            <ion-chip>
                <ion-label>{{due}} {{#str}} itemsdue, mod_rememberme {{/str}}</ion-label>
            </ion-chip>
            {{#hasstreak}}
                <ion-chip color="success">
                    <ion-label>{{streak}} {{#str}} streaklabel, mod_rememberme {{/str}}</ion-label>
                </ion-chip>
            {{/hasstreak}}
        </ion-card-content>
    </ion-card>

    {{#hasquestion}}
    {{#haschoices}}
        {{!
            A single response multiple choice question is a hand of options the
            learner taps. There is no submit button: the tap is the answer. The
            letter on each option becomes the verdict in place once the answer
            is in, so the same element labels the option and then reports on it,
            and colour is never the only thing carrying the result.

            Angular interpolation is avoided throughout in favour of property
            bindings, because this file is rendered through Mustache first and
            the two languages share their braces.
        }}
        <div class="rmm-hand" *ngIf="choices">
            <core-format-text class="rmm-prompt" [text]="choices.questiontext"
                contextLevel="module" [contextInstanceId]="{{cmid}}"></core-format-text>

            <button type="button" class="rmm-choice"
                *ngFor="let choice of choices.choices"
                [class.is-picked]="picked === choice.value"
                [class.is-right]="verdict && choice.value === choices.correctvalue"
                [class.is-wrong]="verdict && picked === choice.value && choice.value !== choices.correctvalue"
                [class.is-faded]="verdict && picked !== choice.value && choice.value !== choices.correctvalue"
                [disabled]="answering || verdict"
                (click)="chooseAnswer(choice.value)">
                <span class="rmm-token" aria-hidden="true" [textContent]="tokenFor(choice)"></span>
                <core-format-text class="rmm-choice-text" [text]="choice.text"
                    contextLevel="module" [contextInstanceId]="{{cmid}}"></core-format-text>
            </button>

            <p class="rmm-verdict" role="status" aria-live="polite" [textContent]="verdictLabel"></p>
        </div>
    {{/haschoices}}
    {{^haschoices}}
        {{!
            The form is this template's job. The app renders the question as
            native controls rather than as the server's HTML, and wraps them in
            nothing, but its answer helper reads a form's elements collection.
            The class is what the accompanying JavaScript anchors on, so that it
            never reads answers out of some other form on the page.
        }}
        <form class="mod_rememberme-question" onsubmit="return false;">
            <core-question
                *ngIf="question"
                [question]="question"
                component="mod_rememberme"
                [componentId]="{{cmid}}"
                contextLevel="module"
                [contextInstanceId]="{{cmid}}"
                preferredBehaviour="immediatefeedback"
                (buttonClicked)="questionButtonClicked($event)"
                (onAbort)="abortQuestion()">
            </core-question>
        </form>

        {{!
            The app pulls the question's own submit button out of the rendered
            HTML and renders it itself, reporting taps through buttonClicked, so
            offering one here as well shows the learner two Check buttons. This
            one is the fallback for a behaviour that extracted none, which would
            otherwise leave the session with no way to answer.
        }}
        <div class="ion-padding" *ngIf="!feedbackShown && !question?.behaviourButtons?.length">
            <ion-button expand="block" (click)="submitAnswer()" [disabled]="submitting">
                {{#str}} checkanswer, mod_rememberme {{/str}}
            </ion-button>
        </div>

        <div class="ion-padding" *ngIf="feedbackShown">
            <ion-button expand="block" fill="outline" (click)="nextQuestion()">
                {{#str}} nextquestion, mod_rememberme {{/str}}
            </ion-button>
        </div>
    {{/haschoices}}
    {{/hasquestion}}

    {{^hasquestion}}
        <ion-card>
            <ion-card-header>
                <ion-card-title>{{#str}} nothingdue, mod_rememberme {{/str}}</ion-card-title>
            </ion-card-header>
            <ion-card-content>
                <p>{{message}}</p>
            </ion-card-content>
        </ion-card>
    {{/hasquestion}}
</div>
